  "description": "A two-bed duplex with a story: the living room is styled as a traditional Irish bar, on one of Dublin's oldest quays in Smithfield, Dublin 7. Bright, 54 sqm, renovated in 2025, with both double bedrooms on their own floor.\n\nMove-in ready: fully furnished, broadband included in the rent from day one, fully equipped kitchen with oven and fridge freezer, bathroom with bathtub, washing machine, dryer and TV. New electric radiators (2025, BER C2). Cot and high chair available on request. A local contact who lives nearby looks after maintenance during the tenancy.\n\nOn your doorstep: Smithfield Square, the Jameson Distillery, the Lighthouse Cinema and the river quays. Temple Bar and the city centre are a short walk across the bridge. Luas Red Line at Smithfield and Four Courts, buses on the quays, Heuston Station 15 minutes on foot.\n\n€2,850 per month. Deposit one month's rent. Available from 1 October, minimum 12-month lease. Non-smoking apartment.\n\nViewings are in person, midweek and weekends. Applicants moving from abroad are welcome to view by representative. To enquire, please include your preferred move-in date and how many people would live in the apartment. Shortlisted applicants will be invited to a viewing and asked for references.",
